1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,960
有多少人订了DVD又不付钱的呢
Well, how many people have ordered DVDs and haven't pay for them.

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:04,800
要是
If...

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,980
我去学校的路上应该有时间绕一下的
I guess I could stop by my way to school.

4
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:08,276
非常非常重要的事
Really really important thing.

5
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:10,960
绮丽儿 我待会打给你
Cheryl? Can I call you back?

6
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:13,120
行 好的 再见
Okay. Great. Bye.

7
00:00:13,150 --> 00:00:14,660
-好了 什么事 -那个
- Yes? What? - Hey, yeah...

8
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:16,320
我刚才仔细检查了浴室你的抽屉
I was going through your drawer in the bathroom

9
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:17,560
找一些唇膏什么的因为我的
looking for some lip stuff because my...

10
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:18,440
嘴唇干了
Lips were dry.

11
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:20,120
-天呐 你真了解我 -菲尔
- God, you know me. - Phil...

12
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:22,820
还记得我们在儿童医院拍到的
Remember the spa certificates we got

13
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:24,740
-温泉疗养券吗 -当然
- at the children's hospital auction? - Mm-hmm.

14
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:27,340
看看 明天就要到期了
Well, look at this -- they expire tomorrow.

15
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:29,514
那你要做什么
Oh, wow. What are you gonna do?

16
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:31,700
克莱尔 我觉得你没有意识到
Claire, I don't think you're grasping the magnitude

17
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,860
这一套服务的价值 这可值两百五十多美元呢
of this package, valued at over $250.

18
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:36,300
-亲爱的 -如果你不用它
- Sweetie... - If you don't use them,

19
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,000
那慈善机构就白拿我们的钱了
then all our money just goes to charity.

20
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:39,660
那我要怎么做
And so what am I supposed to do?

21
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:41,940
在管弦乐队放下艾丽克斯
Somewhere between dropping off Alex at orchestra

22
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,560
再照惯例去去接卢克
and picking up Luke from practice --

23
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:45,980
还烧制一堆才艺表演的DVD的日程之间
oh, and burning a bunch of dvds of the talent show,

24
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:48,660
难道我要跑去做个矿物盐磨砂
I'm gonna, what, pop in for a quick salt scrub?

25
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:50,660
我以为绮丽儿要烧制DVD呢
I thought Cheryl was doing the DVDs.

26
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:51,840
是的 本来是她
Well, she's supposed to,

27
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:53,440
但她就是把这活塞给我了
but somehow she's got me doing it.

28
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:54,380
你应该这样说
Here's what you do.

29
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:56,540
就说 绮丽儿今天我不行
Say, "Cheryl, no can do today.

30
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:57,840
我需要一点属于自己的时间
Need a little 'me time.'"

31
00:00:58,580 --> 00:00:59,480
你见过绮丽儿吗
Have you met Cheryl?

32
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:00,700
那就会变成我的新绰号的
That'll be my new nickname.

33
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:02,640
就叫克莱尔·私人时间·邓菲
I'll be Claire "Me time" Dunphy.

34
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:04,291
这可太不划算了
It's not worth the headache.

35
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:05,100
那就说你病了
Just say you're sick.

36
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:07,300
然后万一我突然撞见她了 那不就彻底穿帮了
Then I run into her, and it'll be a whole thing.

37
00:01:07,380 --> 00:01:08,080
好吧 要是真那样的话
Well, if that happens,

38
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:09,600
你就说你去药店
you say you're on your way to the pharmacy to --

39
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:11,280
菲尔 亲爱的 行不通的
Phil, darling, no, not helping.

40
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,240
好吧 我送给同事弗洛伦斯·刚德曼
Fine. I'll give them to Florence Gunderman at work.

41
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,560
她每次弹班卓琴的时候我都能看见她龟裂的双手
Her hands look gross ever since she took up the banjo.

42
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:18,260
老妈 我要点钱吃午饭
Hey, mom, I need some money for lunch.

43
00:01:18,335 --> 00:01:19,040
我们要去
We're all gonna go to --

44
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:20,620
天呐 把我的线衫脱下来
Oh, my god! Take off my sweater!

45
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:21,780
老妈 叫她脱下来
Mom, tell her to take it off!

46
00:01:21,820 --> 00:01:22,680
艾丽克斯 脱下来
Alex, take it off.

47
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:24,780
上周 她问都没问就穿了我的运动衫
Last week, she wore my sweatshirt without asking.

48
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:25,880
没错
That is true.

49
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:27,820
拜托 那可是抬举
Oh, please -- that was an honor

50
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:29,560
你的破运动衫
for your stupid old sweatshirt.

51
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:31,820
那是它第一次感受胸部的形状
It was the first time the top half got any exercise.

52
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:34,180
老妈 那是我最爱的线衫
Now, mom, that's my favorite sweater!

53
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:35,160
我刚买的
I just got it.

54
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:36,920
你们知道你们这些女生要学什么吗
You know what you girls need to learn to do?

55
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:38,360
你们要学会分享
You need to learn to share,

56
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:40,240
因为那才是姐妹该做的
because that's what sisters do.

57
00:01:40,267 --> 00:01:42,907
行了海莉 你的线衫不会怎样的
All right, Haley, nothing's gonna happen to your sweater.

58
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:43,540
是吧 艾丽克斯
Right, alex?

59
00:01:43,576 --> 00:01:44,791
是吧
Hmm?

60
00:01:44,840 --> 00:01:45,720
行 行
Okay, fine.

61
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:49,660
那我就去穿件你最喜欢的书呆子T恤
Then I will just go put on your favorite nerdy T-shirt,

62
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:52,440
上面有"回到未来"的那件
The one with the guy from "back to the future" on it.

63
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:54,140
那是阿尔伯特·爱因斯坦
That's Albert Einstein!

64
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:56,800
而且一点也不书呆子气
And it is not nerdy!

65
00:01:57,420 --> 00:01:57,840
好吧
Well...

66
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:00,420
你好啊
Hi!

67
00:02:00,467 --> 00:02:02,853
老爸呀 农贸市场怎样呀
Hey, daddy. How was the farmers' market?

68
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:06,020
是不错 但猜猜 新品种菠菜是什么
Well, it was great, but guess what the new spinach is.

69
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:07,360
菊苣吗
Um, radicchio?

70
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:08,600
甘蓝
Kale.

71
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:09,660
不是吧
No!

72
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:12,040
我懂 我当时跟你一样凌乱
I know. I was just as blown away as you are.

73
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:15,600
好吧 我想我们要采用...
Oh, well, I guess we're going to have to adopt --

74
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:16,500
耶
yay --

75
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:17,640
新的态度看待甘蓝了
a new attitude towards kale.

76
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:20,900
可能也要用新的香料
Maybe we'll even adopt a new vinaigrette.

77
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:22,380
用起来用起来
Adopt, yay!

78
00:02:22,380 --> 00:02:24,360
好啦 看看这里怎么啦
Okay, what's going on here?

79
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:26,160
我在运用收养的
I'm taking the negative charge

80
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:27,500
另一层含义 懂吗
out of the word "Adopted." Yay.

81
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:28,960
奥普拉这回又说什么了
What did Oprah do now?

82
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,380
这样的 她有个女儿
Well, she had a girl on

83
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:32,680
十六岁的时候发现自己是收养的
who, at 16, found out that she was adopted

84
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:35,140
她觉得被背叛就跑了 最后变成了脱衣舞女
and felt betrayed, ran away, and became a stripper --

85
00:02:35,174 --> 00:02:38,006
还没在黄金地段 而是机场周边的那种
and not the heart-of-gol kind, the by-the-airport kind.

86
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:38,540
好
Okay.

87
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:41,440
行了 你尽情评论吧 朱迪法官
All right. Go get your gavel, Judge Judy.

88
00:02:41,580 --> 00:02:43,560
不 完全不是 我接受了
No, not at all. I'm adopting

89
00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:47,520
大人不计小人过
A tolerant attitude toward your flights of lunacy.

90
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:48,660
接受[还有领养的意思]
Adopting!

91
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:03,900
艾丽克斯 快点 快点
Alex, come on. Hurry up.

92
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:04,660
我们去的越迟
The later we are,

93
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:06,120
绮丽儿就会发短信叫我做更多的事
the more Cheryl texts me to do.

94
00:03:06,142 --> 00:03:08,278
我来了 来了
I'm coming, I'm coming.

95
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:10,640
再跟我说说这小提琴为什么不跟你一样
Tell me again why the violin just wasn't you.

96
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:11,580
它太高兴了
It's too happy.

97
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:13,980
天呐
Oh, my god!

98
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:15,240
行了 别动别动别动
Okay, hang on. Hang on. Hang on.

99
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:16,620
我看看 应该没什么事
Let's see. It might not be a big deal.

100
00:03:16,688 --> 00:03:19,280
来吧 我来看看
Just -- here we go. Let's see.

101
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:20,960
-好吧 -很糟吗
- Oh, okay. - Is it bad?

102
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:23,400
没事 没事的 你没事的
No, it's gonna be fine. You're gonna be okay.

103
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:24,900
亲爱的
Oh, honey.

104
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:26,840
我忘带手机了
Hey, I forgot my phone.

105
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:27,600
你好啊
Hi.

106
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:28,800
干嘛啊
What?

107
00:03:28,863 --> 00:03:30,777
没事 我爱你
Nothing. I love you.

108
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:31,800
古里古怪的
So weird.

109
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,160
你最好别溅什么东西在上面 知道吗 呆子
You better not spill anything on that, okay, dork?

110
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:37,160
放轻松 这毛衣结实着呢
Relax. Half the 11th grade's been inside this sweater.

111
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:38,920
更重要的是
More than anything

112
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:41,720
我希望我的女儿们不要吵架 亲近一点
I want my girls to stop fighting and be close.

113
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:45,100
我希望他们互相分享衣服 互相做发型
I want them to share clothes and do each other's hair

114
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:46,520
说说男孩子的绯闻
and gossip about boys --

115
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:48,140
就像以前我跟米奇尔那样
like I used to do with Mitchell.

116
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:52,200
歌洛莉亚 走吧 我们走吧
Gloria! Let's go, let's go, let's go!

117
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:55,120
杰 你有没有注意到我走路跳跃了一点
Hey, Jay, have you noticed a spring in my step?

118
00:03:55,180 --> 00:03:56,480
童言无忌
Oh, kids say cruel things.

119
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:58,020
那也不代表你就是那样的
That doesn't mean you'll turn out that way.

120
00:03:58,340 --> 00:04:00,340
不是 我们有相似之处
No. We have something in common.

121
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:01,940
我在和一位小美眉约会
I'm seeing a younger woman.

122
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:03,240
那是有多小
How much younger are we talking about?

123
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:05,360
十三个月 她叫克罗伊
13 months. Her name's Chloe.

124
00:04:05,392 --> 00:04:07,820
她让我感觉自己又是五年级了
She makes me feel like a 5th grader again.

125
00:04:07,820 --> 00:04:08,540
真替你开心 孩子
Good for you, kid.

126
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:13,040
都在啊 我的两个糟老头
Hmm. There they are -- my two dirty old men.

127
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:14,900
拜托 你很快就四十好几的人了
Hey, pretty soon you're gonna be north of 40

128
00:04:15,020 --> 00:04:17,040
我都打算用个更靓的模特换掉你了
and I'm gonna have to trade you in for a newer model.

129
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:17,760
对不 兄弟
Am I right, buddy?

130
00:04:17,810 --> 00:04:20,124
那是我老妈 杰
That's my mother, Jay.

131
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:20,800
准备好了吗
You ready?

132
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:25,000
这么好的天 我们为什么一定要那样做
It's such a beautiful day. Why do we have to do this?

133
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:26,560
因为这事办好了
Because when this thing is behind us,

134
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:28,240
就完事儿了 我们就没有后顾之忧了
It's done and we never have to think about it again.

135
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:28,560
来吧
Come on.

136
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:31,980
我上周六去了个葬礼 我就开始考虑
I went to a funeral last Saturday, and it got me thinking

137
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:34,200
我和歌洛莉亚死后的要葬在哪里
about where Gloria and I were gonna end up after we die.

138
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:36,140
可不是 这一周过得可真太有意思了
Yeah, it's been a fun week.

139
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:37,360
我不喜欢虎头蛇尾
I don't like loose ends.

140
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:38,660
所以我打了几个电话
So I made a few calls.

141
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:41,080
发现在有人在城里最好的墓地
I found these people selling a couple of primo plots

142
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:42,460
出售几块风水宝地
in the best cemetery in town.

143
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:44,440
并不是说我就快入土了
Not that I'm gonna go there anytime soon.

144
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:45,580
别那么肯定
Don't be so sure...

145
00:04:45,626 --> 00:04:47,504
看看他平时吃的那些培根
with all the bacon that he eats.

146
00:04:47,550 --> 00:04:49,774
行了 我吃降胆固醇的药
Well, got to give my cholesterol pills

147
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:51,620
总要有点用处吧
something to do.

148
00:04:54,486 --> 00:04:55,820
我不管他们是怎么促销的
Mm. I don't care how much they promote it,

149
00:04:55,820 --> 00:04:56,660
甘蓝是配菜
kale is a garnish.

150
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:58,400
无法独挑大梁的
It's not ready to anchor a meal.

151
00:04:58,560 --> 00:04:59,380
看看这个
Look at this.

152
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,600
天啊 是我们在越南机场
Oh, my god! Lily's little hat

153
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,120
给莉莉买的小帽子
that we bought her at the airport in Vietnam.

154
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:04,880
还记得她戴着有多可爱吗
Remember how cute she looked in that?

155
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:06,060
还记得我还曾经戴着它走来走去
Remember how I used to wear it

156
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:07,840
表现出好像我有个巨大的脑袋吗
and walk around and act like I had a giant head?

157
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,280
你是实力派
Mm-hmm. That was good acting.

158
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:11,080
你在干什么
So, what are you doing?

159
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:12,940
我在将领养莉莉的过程
I'm putting together a little scrapbook

160
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:14,140
做成剪贴簿
of how Lily became ours.

161
00:05:14,140 --> 00:05:15,940
她的领养证明
You know, her adoption certificate,

162
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:17,360
他们家那个村的几张照片
some pictures of her from her village --

163
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:20,600
全部开诚布公 这样她就不用觉得羞耻了
All out in the open, so she has nothing to be ashamed of.

164
00:05:20,621 --> 00:05:21,888
你还想着这事儿呢
You leaving that on all day?

165
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:23,860
我还要写本小故事书
You know, and I'm also gonna write a little storybook --

166
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:25,260
我可以给她当睡前故事讲
you know, something I can read her at bedtime.

167
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:27,140
就叫"两只猴子和一只熊猫"
It's called "Two monkeys and a panda."

168
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:29,260
她是亚洲人 所以她是熊猫
She's the panda because she's Asian.

169
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:31,840
-我们是猴子是因为 -我只会画猴子
- And we're monkeys because... - I can draw monkeys.

170
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,700
我觉得这是个绝妙的计划
Okay, well, I think this is a great project,

171
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:36,580
我相信你一定会完成的
and I believe you are gonna finish it.

172
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:38,680
-天啊 -怎么了
- Oh, my god. - What?

173
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:41,300
莉莉的领养证明
Lily's adoption certificate.

174
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:43,760
-上面写的是莉莉·塔克·普里契特 -对
- Her name is "Lily Tucker Pritchett." - Right.

175
00:05:43,793 --> 00:05:47,736
而不是"塔克-普里契特" 应该是这个才对
Not "Tucker-Pritchett" like it's supposed to be.

176
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:50,040
名"莉莉" 中间名"塔克"
First name -- "Lily." Middle name -- "Tucker."

177
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:51,160
姓"普里契特"
Last name -- "Pritchett."

178
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:52,500
那肯定不对啊
Well, that can't be right.

179
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:54,380
这可是法律文件
This is a legal document!

180
00:05:55,380 --> 00:05:56,640
她冠的是你的姓
She only has your last name.

181
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:58,450
而我的姓就只是她的中间名
M-m-my name is just a middle name!

182
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:59,720
冷静 别难过
Stay calm. Don't get upset.

183
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:01,600
没有人会知道别人的中间名的
Nobody knows anyone's middle name!

184
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:03,020
-快问快答 我的中间名是什么 -斯考特
- Quick -- what's my middle name? - Scott.

185
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,240
你当然知道我的啦 我们可是一对
Of course you know mine. We're a couple!

186
00:06:04,278 --> 00:06:07,189
这明显是弄错了
Okay, look, t-this is obviously a mistake.

187
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:09,020
但表格是你填的
But you're the one who filled out this paperwork.

188
00:06:09,180 --> 00:06:10,680
你不会犯像这样的错误的
You don't make mistakes like this.

189
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:12,980
一般都是你来改正像这样的错误
You correct mistakes like this.

190
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:16,020
你是故意的
You did this on purpose.

191
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:17,360
什么
What?

192
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:18,900
你把我的名字藏起来
You buried my name,

193
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:20,520
你的姓就可以独霸鳌头
so your name could have top billing.

194
00:06:20,555 --> 00:06:22,322
我才不要听你指责我
Okay, no, I am not gonnsit here and listen

195
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,420
做了这么过分的事情
to you accuse me of something so horrible!

196
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:27,060
现在全都说得通了
It makes so much sense now --

197
00:06:27,060 --> 00:06:29,440
为什么所有法律文件你都想填
Why you wanted to fill out all these legal forms.

198
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:30,600
我是个律师
Okay, well, I'm a lawyer!

199
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:32,400
所以我填写所有法律文件
I fill out all the legal forms,

200
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:35,060
从你签了一个12年的健身会员开始就这样了
ever since you signed up for a 12-year gym membership!

201
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:36,420
会员时间越长 省的就越多
The more you spend, the more you save!

202
00:06:39,807 --> 00:06:42,340
我所有的女同事都没时间去用那张温泉券
All the women I work with are too busy to use the certificate.

203
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:43,840
所以我给温泉那边打了电话
So I called the spa

204
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:46,540
希望他们能延长那张券的有效期
and asked them to extend the expiration date.

205
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:47,720
但他们拒绝了
But they said no.

206
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:49,200
真的要这样么
Really?

207
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,720
他们可真是打错算盘了
Here's something they didn't count on.

208
00:06:52,860 --> 00:06:56,120
你和菲尔·邓菲过不去 你就要吃不了兜着走
You mess with Phil Dunphy, the claws come out.

209
00:06:58,700 --> 00:07:00,740
你的手很好看
You have very nice hands.

210
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:02,399
像女人的手一样柔软
Soft like lady's.

211
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:04,860
谢谢你金 听你这么说我很高兴
Thank you, Kim. I appreciate that.

212
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:07,800
我妻子就好像从未注意过
My wife never seems to notice.

213
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:14,880
就这里了 嗒哒
This is it! Ta-da!

214
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,000
嗒哒什么
What is ta-da?

215
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:19,440
我就是说就在这里了 嗒哒
I'm just saying this is it. Ta-da.

216
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:21,080
"嗒哒"一般是当你按动了开关
"Ta-da" is when you do a flip

217
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:24,480
或者魔术师把个美女一切两半时说的
or where the magician cuts the pretty lady in half,

218
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:26,200
而不是当你给别人展示
not when you show someone

219
00:07:26,243 --> 00:07:28,614
你想把他们的尸体塞进一个什么地方时说的话
where you want to shove their dead body.

220
00:07:28,646 --> 00:07:31,028
我才不和你争论"嗒哒"的正确用法
I'm not gonna argue the proper use of "Ta-da."

221
00:07:31,060 --> 00:07:31,600
就在这里了
This is it.

222
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,940
你认真的么 在这么一堆柜子里面吗
Seriously? In the file cabinet?

223
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:35,240
这叫教堂墓穴
It's called a crypt.

224
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:37,440
你怎么会不懂其中的妙处
And how are you not getting how great this is?

225
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:39,140
我们身处在豪情似海中的古堡中
We're four down from Bugsy siegel.

226
00:07:39,176 --> 00:07:41,352
不 我才不要葬在有墙壁的地方
No. I'm not going into any wall.

227
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:42,560
我会长眠于地下
I'm going in the ground.

228
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:43,480
对不起 我才不要
Sorry, not me.

229
00:07:43,502 --> 00:07:45,126
我才不要死后
There's enough to not like about death

230
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:46,600
还要和泥土和虫子相伴
without adding dirt and worms.

231
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:48,360
那会让我心里一阵阵发毛
The whole thing gives me the willies.

232
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:50,680
你死了 就应该被埋在地下
You die, you go to the ground.

233
00:07:50,712 --> 00:07:53,337
这是自然法则 尘归尘 土归土
Is natural. You go back to the earth.

234
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:55,740
在这里 你就是一袋骨头
Here, you're just a mushy bag of bones

235
00:07:55,740 --> 00:07:57,760
永远都在腐烂
rotting away for all eternity!

236
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:01,740
请您节哀
Sorry for your loss.

237
00:08:02,860 --> 00:08:04,900
我们能赶紧从这出去了吗
Can we get the hell out of here?

238
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:06,540
我该和那个人怎么说
What am I supposed to tell the guy?

239
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:08,720
告诉他们我们才不希望在死后
Tell them we don't want our bodies

240
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:11,460
待在这样上帝无法找到我们的小抽屉里
inside these drawers where god cannot find us!

241
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:12,900
这和咱家的抽屉可不一样
These are not like our drawers at home.

242
00:08:12,980 --> 00:08:14,680
人们可以在这些抽屉里面找到东西
People can find things in these.

243
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:17,040
我想弄个刘海
I'm thinking of getting bangs.

244
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:19,180
你绝对应该弄一个
Ooh, you totally should.

245
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:20,660
你要是有刘海 肯定很美
You would be so cute with bangs.

246
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:22,240
-你的脸型很适合留刘海 我就没有
- You have the face for it. I don't.

247
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:25,180
应该是我老婆
Oh, there's my better half.

248
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:26,200
金 介意帮我接一下吗
Kim, would you mind?

249
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:29,520
亲爱的 你在哪里
Hey, honey. Where are you?

250
00:08:29,740 --> 00:08:31,640
我在去唐尼的路上
Oh, I'm on my way to Downey.

251
00:08:31,712 --> 00:08:33,064
你知道吗
Oh, uh, did you know

252
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:34,900
卡伦和理查德·卡朋特夫妇是在唐尼长大的吗
Karen and richard carpenter grew up in Downey?

253
00:08:34,930 --> 00:08:37,987
你说这事有意义吗 菲尔
What random and not-helpful fact, Phil.

254
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:40,900
对不起 我今天过得不太顺
I'm sorry. I'm -- I'm having kind of a rough day.

255
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:42,960
我过得也不是很顺利
Yeah, I'm kind of having a rough day myself.

256
00:08:45,140 --> 00:08:47,500
菲尔 你得帮我做晚饭了
Look, Phil, I need you to take care of dinner for me.

257
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:48,300
怎么了
What's wrong?

258
00:08:48,356 --> 00:08:50,890
艾莉克斯弄破了海莉的线衫
Oh, Alex ripped Haley's favorite sweater,

259
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,880
现在我就奔波在商店之间
and now I'm driving around from store to store,

260
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:55,100
试图在海莉发现之前给她再买件一模一样的
trying to find the exact same one before Haley finds out.

261
00:08:55,280 --> 00:08:57,780
不用啊 跟她说一下发生了什么就行了
Don't do that. Just explain to her what happened.

262
00:08:57,836 --> 00:08:59,536
不行 海莉不会理解的
Haley's not gonna understand.

263
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:02,420
-她当然会了 -不菲尔 你不明白
- Sure, she will. -- No, phil, you don't understand.

264
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:04,840
我只是想大事化小
I'm trying to avoid this turning into a whole big thing.

265
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:06,500
那就给她买件相似的就成啊
Then just get her something close.

266
00:09:06,580 --> 00:09:07,720
她又看不出来
She'll never know the difference.

267
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:09,760
菲尔 就记住做晚饭好吗亲爱的
Phil, could you just take care of dinner, sweetie?

268
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,040
我就这么点要求 没了
That's all I'm asking. That's it.

269
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:13,500
我只是想说 有更简单的解决方式
I'm just saying, there's a simpler way to do this.

270
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:15,560
没什么更简单的方式 记得做饭
There is no simpler way. Just make dinner!

271
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:16,220
谢谢
Thank you.

272
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:17,180
喂
Hello?

273
00:09:21,940 --> 00:09:22,340
怎么了
What?

274
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:25,100
普里契特先生
Mr. Pritchett...

275
00:09:25,164 --> 00:09:27,712
我们是鲁特莱齐的人
We're the rutledges,

276
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:29,160
就是给你卖墓穴的人
the ones selling the spots.

277
00:09:29,660 --> 00:09:31,040
-你好 -你好
- Hi. - Hi.

278
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:33,060
天啊 看看亲爱的
Oh, my gosh. Look, honey.

279
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:35,700
我都没听说 马丁住进来了
I hadn't heard. Martin is in.

280
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:38,500
瞧瞧啊
Well, look at that.

281
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,860
-不好意思 那是你的朋友吗 -我们只是
- I'm sorry. Is that a friend of yours? - We've made a point

282
00:09:40,860 --> 00:09:42,380
想认识"左邻右舍"的人而已
to get to know everyone in the neighborhood.

283
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:46,200
我们觉得 之后如果在那边遇见不会那么尴尬
We think it makes it less awkward, you know, later.

284
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:47,920
对不起 这位是我妻子 歌洛莉亚
Oh, I'm sorry. This is my wife, Gloria.

285
00:09:50,260 --> 00:09:54,100
我是艾德 这里就是我的位置
I'm Ed, and this is my bunk.

286
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:55,820
这位是我可爱的妻子
And this is my loving wife

287
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:58,340
为三个孩子日夜操劳的母亲 维尼
and devoted mother of three, Winnie.

288
00:09:59,420 --> 00:10:00,440
她会在这里
She'll be here.

289
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:02,400
我还不知道我们要怎么排
I don't know what our lineup is yet.

290
00:10:02,420 --> 00:10:04,760
但在家的时候 我睡在右边
But at home,I sleep on the right side.

291
00:10:04,780 --> 00:10:05,580
所以也许在那里
So probably there.

292
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:07,880
请恕我们无礼
We don't mean to be rude,

293
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:11,200
但你看起来好像比你丈夫年轻很多
but you seem to be much younger than your husband.

294
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:12,940
您不算无礼 我是年轻很多
You're not rude. I'm very much younger.

295
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:13,620
有问题吗
Is that a problem?

296
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:15,880
只是很有可能
Well, it's just that there's a good chance,

297
00:10:15,939 --> 00:10:18,893
你会比她早很久进来
uh, you'll be moving in long before she would.

298
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:22,160
我们关心的是 一旦你妻子改嫁
Our concern is, your wife remarries,

299
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:24,920
而她想又和新丈夫葬在一起
and wants to be laid to rest with her new husband.

300
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:27,580
她就会把这个位置高价卖出
So she sells this spot to the highest bidder.

301
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:30,360
我们就要和一个陌生人做邻居了
And we're left lying next to a complete stranger,

302
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:33,020
甚至连个形式上的招呼都不会和我们打
without even so much as a formal "How do you do?"

303
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:34,440
歌洛莉亚 告诉他们你不会这样
Gloria, tell them you're in.

304
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:38,440
我不知道 杰 我觉得这确实是个问题
I don't know, Jay. I think they have a very good point.

305
00:10:38,980 --> 00:10:41,240
而且他们一点也不荒唐
And they're not crazy at all.

306
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:42,480
你说这话是什么意思
What do you mean they have a good point?

307
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:44,540
我想我们不会选这里了
I don't think this is going to work.

308
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:46,700
希望你们能找到"新邻居"
Good luck getting someone into your drawers.

309
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:54,220
我觉得
It occurs to me

310
00:10:54,220 --> 00:10:56,580
我可能有点过于不安了
that I may have gotten a little too upset

311
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:59,240
还得出了某些
and jumped to some conclusions

312
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:00,900
或许不正确的结论
that were perhaps not true.

313
00:11:01,520 --> 00:11:03,260
我现在意识到
I realize now that you would

314
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:06,660
你绝对不会故意做出如此荒唐的事情
never intentionally do something so unthinkable.

315
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:07,700
所以
So...

316
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:12,100
我想说 我很抱歉 我指责了你
I just wanted to say I'm sorry for accusing you.

317
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:13,140
我确实做了
I did it.

318
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:14,759
我就知道 你个两面派
I knew it! You two-faced --

319
00:11:14,807 --> 00:11:16,492
听我解释 那是
Let me explain. There is --

320
00:11:16,520 --> 00:11:18,752
解释就是掩饰 掩饰就是一切罪恶的开始
There is no explanation. There is just no excuse.

321
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:20,260
我只想知道为什么
I just want to know why!

322
00:11:20,289 --> 00:11:23,560
你知道吗 有些女人说
Okay, y-you know how, um, s-some women say

323
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:25,820
她们忘了生孩子有多痛苦
that they forget how painful childbirth was?

324
00:11:25,846 --> 00:11:28,105
我想你是忘了
Well, I-I-I think that you are forgetting

325
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:30,300
在领养莉莉之前你有多惊慌失措
how panicked you were before we got Lily.

326
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:32,380
-你完全抓狂了 -我没有
- You were freaking out. - I was not!

327
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:35,200
这上面说床垫
Okay, so, it says that we can put the mattress

328
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:36,600
有三种不同的放法
at one of three different levels.

329
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:38,540
-我们应该选哪一个呢 -我不知道
- Which one should we do? - I don't know.

330
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:40,220
好吧 那想想我们应该把她放在多深的位置
Well, just think about how far down she should be.

331
00:11:40,260 --> 00:11:42,593
-多深 -我不知道 我不能做这个
- How far -- - I don't know! I can't do this!

332
00:11:44,837 --> 00:11:46,942
好的
Okay.

333
00:11:46,972 --> 00:11:48,860
这个弹簧固定系统真是太棒了
Oh, this latch system is great.

334
00:11:48,860 --> 00:11:49,920
真不知道以前的人是怎么固定的
What did people do before this?

335
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:51,900
我不知道 别问我问题
I don't know! Stop asking me questions!

336
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:53,900
-小卡 -我不能做这个 我不能
- Cam... - I can't do this! I can't!

337
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:57,000
好吧 我
Okay, well, I...

338
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,600
我可不觉得这两件事之间有什么联系
I don't see what that has to do with anything.

339
00:11:58,646 --> 00:12:01,466
我很害怕这件事
I-I was scared that -- that it was just gonna all be

340
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:03,640
你承受不了 我怕你会离开我
too much for you and that you were gonna leave.

341
00:12:04,180 --> 00:12:06,900
我就会成为一个单身爸爸
And then I would be the one taking care of a baby

342
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:08,200
带着的孩子还跟一个
and half of her last name

343
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,200
弃我而去的人姓
would belong to the guy who left us.

344
00:12:12,220 --> 00:12:13,860
是我做错了 我很抱歉
It was a mistake. I'm sorry.

345
00:12:13,902 --> 00:12:15,309
我本想挽回的
I-I wanted to have it changed,

346
00:12:15,340 --> 00:12:16,660
但是我需要你的签名
but I needed to get your signature,

347
00:12:16,660 --> 00:12:19,080
我怕这会让我们大吵一架
and I was afraid that it would start a big fight

348
00:12:19,129 --> 00:12:20,429
会让你讨厌我 然后
and that you would hate me and...

349
00:12:24,260 --> 00:12:25,120
那我就不明白了
OK, I'm confused.

350
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:27,300
你们是说 如果她告诉我她有了麻烦
You're saying that if she tells me she has a problem,

351
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:28,500
我却不该帮助她
I'm not supposed to help her?

352
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:30,600
除非她求你帮她
Not unless she asks for your help.

353
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:31,920
但如果她让我帮助她了
But if she lets me help her,

354
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:33,300
她就不会有麻烦了啊
I can make her problem go away.

355
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:36,580
那是你们男人的观点
That is such a male thing to say.

356
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:38,420
请原谅我是个男人
Well, forgive me for being a man.

357
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:40,580
芒果的还是猕猴桃的
Mango or kiwi?

358
00:12:40,612 --> 00:12:42,097
猕猴桃的
Ooh, kiwi.

359
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:44,960
当你说应该如何如何做时
When you say, you know, "Do this or do that,"

360
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:47,760
她会觉得你是在说"我比你聪明多了"
all she's hearing is, "I'm smarter than you."

361
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,380
相信我 她不会这么想的
Believe me, she doesn't think that.

362
00:12:49,426 --> 00:12:52,459
她不希望你替他解决麻烦
She doesn't want you to save her problems.

363
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:54,280
她只希望得到你的支持
She just wants you to give her support

364
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:56,100
让她自己解决麻烦
so that she can solve her problems herself.

365
00:12:56,380 --> 00:12:58,060
没错 而且有时候
Yes, and sometimes --

366
00:12:58,260 --> 00:13:00,540
有时候她只需要一个倾诉的对象
sometimes she just wants a sympathetic ear.

367
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:04,960
或许这才问题的关键
Maybe it's all the creams,

368
00:13:04,980 --> 00:13:06,540
但说的很有道理 姑娘们
but that just made sense, girlfriends.

369
00:13:07,460 --> 00:13:11,160
那么如果克莱尔说 我讨厌堵车
So if Claire says, "I hate getting stuck in traffic,"

370
00:13:11,201 --> 00:13:14,746
-我就不该说 你应该早点出门 -不
- I shouldn't say, "Maybe you should leave earlier"... - No.

371
00:13:14,777 --> 00:13:16,715
-或是 别上高速公路 -不
- ...Or, "Don't get on the freeway." - No.

372
00:13:16,747 --> 00:13:20,519
我应该说 我懂 这是挺郁闷的
I should just say, "I know. It's so frustrating."

373
00:13:20,540 --> 00:13:21,660
-是的 这就对了 -真的吗
- Yes! That's it! - Really?

374
00:13:21,698 --> 00:13:22,639
没错
Yes! Yes!

375
00:13:22,662 --> 00:13:24,157
如果她说
And -- and if she says, uh, uh...

376
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:26,980
今天的服务员态度太差了
"The waiter I had today was so rude,"

377
00:13:27,019 --> 00:13:29,073
我不该说 你应该一次性
I shouldn'say, "Maybe you should just order

378
00:13:29,102 --> 00:13:30,931
-把菜全点好 -不行
- something on the menu for once." - No.

379
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:33,720
我应该说 真混蛋
I should just say, "What a jerk."

380
00:13:33,749 --> 00:13:34,859
对了 就是这样
Yes! Yes! Yeah!

381
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:38,380
如果她说 菲尔 这节目快把我逼疯了
And if she says, "Phil, the TV's driving me crazy,"

382
00:13:38,420 --> 00:13:39,840
我应该说 我知道
I should just say, "I know!

383
00:13:39,882 --> 00:13:42,689
现在的电视节目都不是人看的
There is not enough quality programming for men."

384
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:45,080
不 你应该关掉那该死的电视
No! Turn off the damn TV.

385
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:47,840
好吧 我又不明白了
Okay, now I'm confused again.

386
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:51,820
听说你今天过的不太愉快啊
So, I heard you had a rough time today.

387
00:13:52,380 --> 00:13:53,200
是啊
Yeah, well...

388
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:55,360
还记得那些我们以为会永远在一起的日子吗
Remember the days when we thought we'd live forever?

389
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:56,680
你想去玩吗
Don't you want to go play?

390
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:57,820
我什么时候玩过
When do I ever play?

391
00:13:58,840 --> 00:13:59,560
我似乎也得应付
I'm kind of wrestling

392
00:13:59,590 --> 00:14:01,820
这些老夫少妻的事
with this whole "older man, younger woman" thing.

393
00:14:01,860 --> 00:14:03,680
就好像我和克罗伊的生活背景不同
It's like Chloe and I grew up in different worlds.

394
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:05,580
今天我说了个关于威格尔家的笑话
Today I made a joke about the Wiggles.

395
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:08,100
-她居然一头雾水 -我不知道你说的什么
- It went right over her head. - I don't know what that is.

396
00:14:08,180 --> 00:14:10,800
这是个短语 意思就是她不明白
It's an expression -- means she didn't get it.

397
00:14:12,588 --> 00:14:14,510
是啊 有时候年龄的事
Yeah, it sometimes -- this age thing --

398
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:16,080
是很让人心烦
knocks you in the head.

399
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:17,540
你是指什么呢
That what this is about?

400
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:21,200
我一直都明白 我去世之后你妈可能会改嫁
I always knew your mother might remarry after I'm gone.

401
00:14:21,220 --> 00:14:22,080
可我从来没烦恼过
That never bothered me.

402
00:14:22,180 --> 00:14:24,980
她嫁过你爸 嫁过我
I figured her husbands would be your dad, me,

403
00:14:25,140 --> 00:14:27,780
肯定也会嫁某些完全比不上我的傻瓜
and some putz who could never live up to me.

404
00:14:27,808 --> 00:14:29,581
但如果我不是她心中最重要的那一个怎么办
But what if I'm not the main guy?

405
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:31,120
如果她更爱其他人
What if some other guy is?

406
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:33,120
如果我才是那个傻瓜
What if I'm the putz?

407
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:35,460
我妈和我爸离婚的时候
When my mom and dad got divorced,

408
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:38,280
你知道有多少人在追求她吗
do you have any idea how many guys chased after her?

409
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:40,440
电话铃声就没停过
The phone didn't stop ringing.

410
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:41,900
那些人会半路把她拦住
Men would stop her on the street.

411
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:44,320
车还没停下 就向她求婚
Guys would propose to her from moving cars.

412
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,960
他们都长得很帅 又多金
They were good-looking guys, Jay -- with money.

413
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:48,960
我觉得他们中的一个能当总统
I think one of them was a Kennedy.

414
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:49,980
你说这些是什么意思
Where are you going with this?

415
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:52,660
当你出现的时候 我觉得你没什么希望
When you showed up, I didn't think you had a prayer.

416
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,780
你紧张得大汗淋漓的 我真为感到难过
You were so nervous and sweaty, I felt sorry for you.

417
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:57,800
我可是被迫爬了三段楼梯
I had to climb three flights of stairs.

418
00:14:57,840 --> 00:15:00,469
但在所有人中 我妈选中了你
But of all people, my mom fell for you.

419
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:01,720
她追姑娘很有一手
I got a few moves.

420
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:04,000
她说第一次和你吵架的时候就爱上你了
She said she fell in love with you during your first fight.

421
00:15:04,041 --> 00:15:06,838
-什么 -她说她终于找到了真命天子
- What? - She said she'd finally met her match.

422
00:15:06,869 --> 00:15:08,464
是嘛
Oh.

423
00:15:09,572 --> 00:15:11,240
所以如果你认为她会在你去世后
So if you think she's just gonna replace you

424
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:11,860
找人代替你
when you're gone,

425
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:13,300
那你就是个傻瓜
Then you are the putz.

426
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:16,820
谢谢你 孩子 醍醐灌顶啊
Thanks, kid.I appreciate that.

427
00:15:18,020 --> 00:15:19,380
我还以为一开始你就喜欢我
I thought you liked me when I first showed up.

428
00:15:19,580 --> 00:15:20,980
拜托 头一个月
Please. For the first month,

429
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,600
我甚至都不想知道你的名字
I didn't even bother to learn your name.

430
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:27,120
-她回来了吗 -在路上了
- Is she back yet? - She's on her way.

431
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:28,520
-你找到了吗 -找到了
- Did you find it? - I did.

432
00:15:28,520 --> 00:15:30,340
终于在第五家店找到了
At the fifth store I went to.

433
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:32,520
就在橱窗里 我是从模特身上扒下来的
It was in the window, and I had to undress a mannequin

434
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:33,920
还被一个变态拍了下来
while a creepy guy filmed it,

435
00:15:33,920 --> 00:15:35,460
我们估计能在网上找到
So we have to look forward to on the internet.

436
00:15:35,980 --> 00:15:37,860
-太谢谢你了 妈妈 -不谢
- Thank you so much, mom. - You're welcome.

437
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,160
现在 快放到它原来的地方去 知道吗
Now, go put that exactly where you found the other one, okay?

438
00:15:40,192 --> 00:15:41,655
好的
Okay.

439
00:15:43,300 --> 00:15:44,100
啊欧
Uh-oh.

440
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,560
-什么 -防盗扣还在上面呢
- What? The security tag -- it's still on!

441
00:15:46,620 --> 00:15:48,200
我跟他们说了让他们取下来
I told those people to take that off.

442
00:15:48,238 --> 00:15:50,662
-不 -她已经开入停车道了
- Oh, no. - She's pulling into the driveway!

443
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:51,580
好的 没事 没事
Okay. It's fine. It's fine.

444
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:52,760
别紧张 快弄好了 快弄好了
Don't panic. I've got it. I've got it.

445
00:15:52,792 --> 00:15:55,132
-她下车了 -别闹了 我正在弄
- She's getting out of the car! - All right! I am doing it!

446
00:15:55,175 --> 00:15:57,579
快弄好了 我 哦 天啊 糟了
I've almost got it. I -- oh, god! Oh, no!

447
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:59,680
-什么东西 -是墨水
- What is that?! - Well, it's ink.

448
00:15:59,707 --> 00:16:01,384
藏起来 快藏起来
Aah! Hide it. Hide it.

449
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:04,560
-她进来了 -你把我毛衣怎么了
- She's in the house! - What are you doing with my sweater?

450
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:05,900
天啊 你把它毁了
Oh, my god! It's ruined!

451
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:07,100
只是个意外
It was an accident!

452
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:09,140
我就知道会这样 你个笨蛋
I knew this would happen, you idiot!

453
00:16:09,220 --> 00:16:11,080
嘿 嘿 有话好好说
Hey, hey! Let's try to get along.

454
00:16:11,090 --> 00:16:12,918
我真希望她根本没生下来过
I wish she was never even born!

455
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:15,320
他们只不过需要一个有脑子的孩子
They were trying to make one with a brain!

456
00:16:15,374 --> 00:16:17,671
别乱讲 亲爱的 你们都很
Not fair! Honey, you guys are both...

457
00:16:17,714 --> 00:16:20,625
都很聪明
Oh...pretty smart.

458
00:16:20,658 --> 00:16:22,351
噢
Ohh...

459
00:16:22,383 --> 00:16:24,399
天啊
Geez.

460
00:16:24,442 --> 00:16:26,308
是线衫的事对吧
It's that sweater, huh?

461
00:16:26,340 --> 00:16:28,486
对 就是线衫的事
Yeah. It is that sweater.

462
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:30,800
我尽了一切努力避免她们吵架
And I did everything I can to stop them from fighting.

463
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:32,340
我就不懂了
I don't understand.

464
00:16:32,340 --> 00:16:34,620
她们怎么没意识到你有多么爱她们
Why they can't see how much you love them.

465
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:35,700
我也不懂
I don't know.

466
00:16:35,733 --> 00:16:38,380
还有今天绮丽儿一直给我打电话
Meanwhile, Cheryl has be calling me all day

467
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:40,200
就因为她生气我没去
because she's angry I didn't show up.

468
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:42,440
绮丽儿家里不是有管家和保姆什么的吗
Doesn't Cheryl have a housekeeper and a nanny?

469
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:44,180
为什么她还要别人帮忙
Why does she need so much help?

470
00:16:44,940 --> 00:16:45,880
我也知道 你说是吧
I know, right?

471
00:16:46,060 --> 00:16:47,600
你鞠躬尽瘁
You work so hard.

472
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:49,580
你劳苦功高
You do so much.

473
00:16:50,100 --> 00:16:50,820
对啊
I do.

474
00:16:51,980 --> 00:16:52,920
百分之百对
Of course you do.

475
00:16:53,340 --> 00:16:54,160
确实
I do.

476
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:55,920
确实
I do.

477
00:16:58,220 --> 00:17:00,560
亲爱的 谢谢你
Oh, sweetie, thank you.

478
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:02,680
真的很感谢
I really appreciate that.

479
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:05,480
嘿
Hey.

480
00:17:05,940 --> 00:17:06,660
什么
Yeah?

481
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:08,060
我老婆是谁
Who's my gal?

482
00:17:08,760 --> 00:17:09,700
就是我
I am.

483
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:10,820
答对了 就是你
Darn right. Yeah.

484
00:17:12,988 --> 00:17:14,396
我去洗个手
Oh. Let me get this.

485
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:15,380
嘿 还有一件事
Hey, by the way --

486
00:17:16,340 --> 00:17:17,340
发现我有什么不同吗
notice anything different about me?

487
00:17:17,399 --> 00:17:20,781
没啊
Unh-unh.

488
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:21,240
哈
Huh.

489
00:17:21,297 --> 00:17:24,484
哪里不同了
Hmm. What is it?

490
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:24,880
没什么
Nothing.

491
00:17:25,360 --> 00:17:27,320
-剪头发了吗 -一个礼拜前就剪了
- A haircut? - A week ago.

492
00:17:27,320 --> 00:17:28,960
好啦 快点告诉我
Okay, so, tell me.

493
00:17:29,780 --> 00:17:31,140
算了 没什么重要的
Forget it. It's not important.

494
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:33,140
我去做饭了
Okay. I'll just go start dinner.

495
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:37,240
听着 我想了想
Listen, I've been thinking.

496
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:40,080
在我死了以后
When I go,

497
00:17:40,220 --> 00:17:41,680
我想告诉你
I want you to know...

498
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:44,840
你嫁给别人也可以的
It's okay if you marry someone else.

499
00:17:45,060 --> 00:17:45,860
我知道
I know.

500
00:17:47,180 --> 00:17:48,760
因为我想你幸福
Because I want you be happy.

501
00:17:49,220 --> 00:17:50,040
我会幸福的
I'll be happy.

502
00:17:50,072 --> 00:17:52,200
你故意气我是不是
You're driving me crazy on purpose, right?

503
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:54,440
杰 我不会嫁给别人的
Jay, I'm not going to marry anyone else.

504
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:55,420
你现在是这么说的
That's what you say now,

505
00:17:55,420 --> 00:17:57,280
但是没人知道未来是怎样的
but no one knows what the future holds.

506
00:17:57,620 --> 00:17:59,120
所以我给你这个
So I want you to have this.

507
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:01,180
看这个
Look at this,

508
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:03,160
一个空的咖啡罐
an empty coffee can.

509
00:18:03,940 --> 00:18:05,980
你知道追我的男人给我买什么吗
Do you know what men used to buy me?

510
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:08,720
我死了以后 把我火化了
When I go, toss me in the fire,

511
00:18:08,750 --> 00:18:10,820
把我的骨灰放进这个罐子里面
Sweep up my ashes, stick 'em in that.

512
00:18:11,420 --> 00:18:11,820
嗒哒
Ta-da!

513
00:18:12,820 --> 00:18:14,720
我得跟你谈一谈这个"嗒哒"
We need to talk about this "Ta-da."

514
00:18:16,079 --> 00:18:19,030
因为我不在乎我死后待的地方有没有墙
'Cause I don't care if it's in a wall

515
00:18:19,060 --> 00:18:20,560
或者还是被深埋地下
or if it's in the ground --

516
00:18:21,140 --> 00:18:22,600
我只要和你在一起就行了
just as long as I end up with you.

517
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:24,520
哦 杰
Oh, Jay.

518
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:28,300
太完美了
It's perfect.

519
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:32,620
杰·普里契特的骨灰咖啡罐放在壁橱上
Jay Pritchett sitting on the mantel in the old coffee can.

520
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:35,600
这些追求者就傻眼了 我就喜欢这样
That will drive the putz crazy. And I like that.

521
00:18:43,768 --> 00:18:46,992
所以说 我左思右想
Um, so, f-for whatever it's worth,

522
00:18:47,033 --> 00:18:48,980
我还是叫来了收养律师
I-I called the adoption attorney --

523
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:50,040
收养 耶
Adoption, yay!

524
00:18:50,050 --> 00:18:52,854
在星期一 他们就会开始着手准备
And on Monday, they're gonna start the process

525
00:18:52,883 --> 00:18:56,011
把莉莉的姓改成塔克-普里契特
of changing lily's last name to "Tucker-pritchett."

526
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:56,580
好啊
Great.

527
00:18:56,636 --> 00:19:01,358
我想再次道歉
Again, I'm -- I'm so sorry.

528
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:03,980
好吧
Okay.

529
00:19:04,879 --> 00:19:06,730
这个 我
Um... Oh, I, uh...

530
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:11,680
我刚写完了《两只猴和一只熊猫》
I took a quick pass at "Two Monkeys and a Panda."

531
